": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01", "start": 298, "end": 498, "text": "The death notice from the \"State Gazette of South-Carolina\" (SC), June 18, 1790, described him as a \"tender husband and parent, humane master, steady unshaken patriot, the gentleman, and the scholar.\""}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01", "start": 499, "end": 585, "text": "The plantation then passed to Henry, his eldest son, later Governor of South Carolina."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 0, "end": 16, "text": "Sarah Middleton."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 17, "end": 121, "text": "Middleton’s father died in 1685, leaving to his wife, Sara, and their young son, Arthur, the plantation."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 122, "end": 289, "text": "In the following decade, English colonists learned how to cultivate rice in fresh water swamps, with slave labor, by 1699, The Oaks plantation had begun to make money."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 290, "end": 376, "text": "By 1720, the estate consisted of over 5,000 acres and Middleton owned over 100 slaves."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 377, "end": 465, "text": "A well-established member of the Carolina gentry, Middleton was also a respected member."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 466, "end": 548, "text": "In 1710, he traveled to London to discuss the political problems in the Carolinas."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "start": 549, "end": 603, "text": "Middleton died on September 17, 1737 at the age of 56,"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "start": 0, "end": 158, "text": "Arthur Edward Middleton Arthur Edward Middleton (2 November 1891 – 19 October 1953) was a British politician who served as the Chair of London County Council."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "start": 159, "end": 278, "text": "Middleton qualified as an accountant and served on the council of the Society of Incorporated Accountants and Auditors."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "start": 279, "end": 385, "text": "He was a supporter of the Labour Party, and in 1942 was appointed to London County Council as an alderman."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "start": 386, "end": 505, "text": "In 1946, he was elected to represent Islington North on the council, and then from 1952 he again served as an alderman."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "start": 506, "end": 566, "text": "In addition, he served on the Royal Commission on the Press."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "start": 567, "end": 581, "text": "In April 1953,"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d00:c0", "entity": "Arthur Middleton", "scope": "death date", "claim": "Arthur Middleton died on January 1, 1787.", "answer": "January 1, 1787", "quote": "Middleton died on January 1, 1787 at the age of 44 and was buried in the family tomb in the Gardens at Middleton Place.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d01:c0", "entity": "Arthur Middleton", "scope": "death date", "claim": "Arthur Middleton died on June 15, 1790.", "answer": "June 15, 1790", "quote": "Middleton died on June 15, 1790 at the age of 47 and was buried in the family tomb in the Gardens at Middleton Place.", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02", "card_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d02:c0", "entity": "Arthur Middleton", "scope": "death date", "claim": "Arthur Middleton died on September 17, 1737.", "answer": "September 17, 1737", "quote": "Middleton died on September 17, 1737 at the age of 56,", "original_document_number": 3}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0424-54085d7b43ca:d03:c0", "entity": "Arthur Middleton", "scope": "death date", "claim": "Arthur Middleton died on 19 October 1953.", "answer": "19 October 1953", "quote": "Arthur Edward Middleton Arthur Edward Middleton (2 November 1891 – 19 October 1953) was a British politician who served as the Chair of London County Council.", "original_document_number": 4}], "current_answers": ["January 1, 1787", "June 15, 1790", "September 17, 1737", "19 October 1953"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "January 1, 1787", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "June 15, 1790", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "September 17, 1737", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R3", "answer": "19 October 1953", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
